WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Local models just matched a frontier coding agent on five real tasks while running on a single

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:13.560
16-gigabyte card. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 207. A local Lama bakeoff on an RX-9060 XT ask

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:20.540
nine models to write solution.py and test underscore solution.py. Execute the tests and clear

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:28.340
performance gate. Deepseek V4.1 flash from the cloud and QN 3.827B UDIQ4

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:34.680
underscore XS with MTP both scored 5 out of 5. The remaining 7 models failed at

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.220
least one of the interval scheduling or shortest prefix tasks. The problems

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.780
covered CSV quoting rules and arithmetic evaluator with pinned exceptions,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:50.880
A POSIX-ish shell tokenizer, max-profit interval scheduling with tie breaks on 200,000 intervals,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.720
and shortest prefix pattern matching against 4,000 characters.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.160
Both perfect runs used a Thompson NFA with Epsilon closure on the last task,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.160
and a bisect dynamic program on the scheduler.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.140
The QN variant burned 185,000 tokens over 94 minutes,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.440
while the cloud deep-seek finished in 236 seconds on 43,000 tokens.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.740
And most of that local time went into a 9,000-case fuzz after the model had already reported success.

00:01:20.628 --> 00:01:26.068
Nvidia shipped structured data models, a pie-torch library that Mark Techposts as exposes

00:01:26.068 --> 00:01:30.008
pre-trained tabular foundation models for predictions with no training step.

00:01:30.508 --> 00:01:36.688
The library wraps tab ICL, V2, and Kumo tabular for single tables plus Kumo relational for

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:42.788
full relational databases, and each model answers in context, taking labeled rows and query

00:01:42.788 --> 00:01:44.568
rows through a single forward pass.

00:01:45.288 --> 00:01:50.488
Users can reuse and encoded contacts across many queries, read calibrated intervals on

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:53.188
regression heads, and scale to 20 class problems.

00:01:53.768 --> 00:01:58.788
The tutorial walks through type table tensors, a comparison against scikit-learn baselines,

00:01:59.428 --> 00:02:04.268
a three table shop database, and pre-processing pitfalls such as drop timestamp columns.

00:02:04.928 --> 00:02:09.908
Install needs a pinned git commit, since the package builds wheel URLs that do not match

00:02:09.908 --> 00:02:13.308
the Torch Miner version PieGib lib wheels actually published.

00:02:13.828 --> 00:02:18.628
The relational sampler path needs the PieGib lib wheel built for the exact major minor

00:02:18.628 --> 00:02:22.408
Torch version, rather than the patch version the library hard codes.

00:02:23.402 --> 00:02:29.562
DeepSeek released the 1017 checkpoint of V4.1 Flash, a major revision that local LAMA

00:02:29.562 --> 00:02:31.882
users are already wiring into dwarf star.

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:39.082
The update changed roughly 40% of routed expert tensors, 30% of Ngrams, and 50% of vision

00:02:39.082 --> 00:02:45.962
tower experts while keeping the same architecture. A mixed Q2 to Q8 quant following anti-resas original

00:02:45.962 --> 00:02:53.722
dwarf star recipe now fits the 152 gigabyte wired backbone, plus a 200 gigabyte engram table on 128

00:02:53.722 --> 00:03:00.682
gigabyte systems with SSD streaming. The AMATrix calibration was rebuilt from the 1017 checkpoint

00:03:00.682 --> 00:03:05.822
rather than the original weights. Early tests show the model remains competitive as the leading

00:03:05.822 --> 00:03:09.382
open-weights release, and the end-gram table pages on demand.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:17.890
Voxel 51 3.0 unifies search, curation, annotation, and evaluation for multi-modal sensor data aimed

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:22.470
at robotics, vehicles, and factory teams, Mark Tech Post reports.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:30.670
The release ships Voxel 51 agent with 45-plus model context protocol, or MCP tools, 80-plus

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:35.850
operators and 18 open source skills, plus data set versioning and a free tier that

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.650
allows three data sets of 10,000 samples each.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:44.090
Time series support now aligns multiple sensor streams on one timeline with segment level

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:44.670
embeddings.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:53.030
Supported modalities include MCAP, Images, Video, 3D point clouds, meshes, DICOM, NIFTI,

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.010
Geospatial data and audio.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:04:02.090
Voxel 51 Search uses a lasting hybrid index on Lance DB that mixes Vector, Scaler, and

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.770
full-text retrieval, and it skips full rebuilds when data arrives incrementally.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:12.310
The free tier caps storage at 20GB and inference at 30,000 requests per month.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:18.494
Anthropic is enlisting legal expertise, the Financial Times reports, so AI agents can

00:04:18.494 --> 00:04:21.074
negotiate and execute contracts autonomously.

00:04:21.074 --> 00:04:26.594
The work targets the practical gap between agent capability and enforceable commercial agreements.

00:04:27.531 --> 00:04:33.591
Early support for the emerging IDJag identity standard is going into Octa's cross-app access solution

00:04:33.591 --> 00:04:38.551
ahead of formal internet engineering task force, or IETF standardization.

00:04:39.071 --> 00:04:45.591
The work lets autonomous agents authenticate across APIs and enterprise workflows, simply Wall Street ads,

00:04:45.911 --> 00:04:49.031
using the same identity layer that already serves human users.

00:04:49.031 --> 00:04:55.171
Acta's early implementation gives it influence over default patterns before the standard is finalized.

00:04:55.491 --> 00:05:02.511
And the company is aligning IDJAG usage with existing cross-app access and auth0 for AI agents products.

00:05:03.131 --> 00:05:10.271
A 5070 Ti paired with a 3070 on a PCIe riser now runs Quinn 3.635 BA3

00:05:10.671 --> 00:05:17.451
at 82 tokens a second with 16,000 context using Olama or llama.cpp layer splitting.

00:05:17.451 --> 00:05:23.571
a local LAMA builder posted. Roughly 23% of layers spill into system RAM while the

00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:30.731
3070 keeps 4GB unused. The 5070 TI was purchased for $750 after tax in

00:05:30.731 --> 00:05:36.371
November 2025. Layer splitting works because the riser runs at X1 and the split

00:05:36.371 --> 00:05:40.931
passes very little data between cards, and the user has not yet tuned the split

00:05:40.931 --> 00:05:47.490
ratio between the two GPUs. A VLLM backed controller on local LAMA uses Motherboard

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:52.910
temperature sensors to modulate GPU load as a space heater, pausing inference when heating

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:58.770
is active and exposing a token gated local host UI. The project is released as a sanitized

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:04.270
public repo focused on the control loop rather than production use. The system pauses heating

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:09.050
during inference and accepts target temperature commands from a partner via the gated web page.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:16.350
It is built around the user's existing VLLM backend, and an ESP32-based thermostat is planned next.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:22.778
Red Curtain Port's Fish Audio Drama 3, a 35 billion mixture of experts model with about

00:06:22.778 --> 00:06:29.378
3 billion active to an RX-9070 by keeping FP8 experts in system RAM and caching only

00:06:29.378 --> 00:06:30.638
active ones on the card.

00:06:31.098 --> 00:06:37.818
It produces 3.3 seconds of speech in 13 seconds while using 11 to 12 gigabytes of VRAM against

00:06:37.818 --> 00:06:43.138
an official ask of a 48-gigabyte Nvidia card, according to that local AMA write-up.

00:06:43.138 --> 00:06:48.958
The port keeps top-k off, supplies each speaker with a reference voice clip, and avoids starting

00:06:48.958 --> 00:06:50.238
lines with sound tags.

00:06:50.738 --> 00:06:55.478
A small web UI supports voice cloning from a reference clip and multi-speaker scripts

00:06:55.478 --> 00:06:58.038
with the same tags used in Fish's own editor.

00:06:58.678 --> 00:07:03.538
The first line sometimes plays then goes silent, matching a known behavior in the original

00:07:03.538 --> 00:07:04.778
VLLM recipe.

00:07:04.778 --> 00:07:15.340
Unsloth IQ-4XS with key value cache streaming and N-gram prediction ran QN-3.827B at 262,000

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:20.200
context on 24GB of system RAM, another local LAMMA post showed.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:27.460
The setup delivered 42.7 tokens a second in generation and 658 in pre-fill at 20,000

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:33.720
context, using a fork of LAMMA.CPP that needed a GROCC-assisted fix for missing PCIe

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:41.100
At 200,000 context, the same hardware sustains 35 tokens a second in generation and 500 in

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.540
pre-fill.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:46.660
The user runs the model with Q4 key value cache values and Q8 keys.

00:07:47.657 --> 00:07:52.357
If you want a reality check, rerun that 9 model coding gauntlet on whatever card you

00:07:52.357 --> 00:07:55.777
already have and see which checkpoint actually finishes without hanging.

00:07:56.417 --> 00:08:00.977
Grab and video structure data models from the GitHub commit named in the tutorial and

00:08:00.977 --> 00:08:04.317
and throw your own three-table shop database at the zero-shot path.

00:08:04.697 --> 00:08:10.837
If you need multi-speaker cloning without a 48GB NVIDIA GPU, try the red curtain port

00:08:10.837 --> 00:08:13.517
of Fish Audio Drama 3 on an AMD card.

00:08:14.057 --> 00:08:21.857
Load the 1017 Deepseek V4.1 flash-quant in dwarf star on 128GB hardware and compare vision

00:08:21.857 --> 00:08:24.117
and language quality against the prior checkpoint.

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:30.004
More community quants of the 1017 Deepseek checkpoint are expected in the next few days.

00:08:30.004 --> 00:08:35.484
additional MCP tool packs for Voxel 51 agent will appear as robotics teams

00:08:35.484 --> 00:08:40.504
publish their workflows. Further mismatched GPU split ratio experiments will

00:08:40.504 --> 00:08:46.980
surface as 5070 TI owners add older cards. Idle time on a five device chain is the

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:51.660
reason to pop the hood on pipeline speculation for mixed kits. Multi-device

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:55.680
mixture of experts inference looks like simple layer sharding until the slowest

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.740
link leaves 4 or 5 gadgets waiting.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:02.760
The practical fix is a small draft head on the first device that guesses the next few

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:06.660
tokens, after which the entire chain validates them in one pass.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.880
That first device then starts the next speculation while earlier guesses are still traveling.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:17.400
A verified step averages about 2.2 tokens, so the weight becomes decode.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:24.900
On a 48-layer 512-expert model split across two PCs, an M4 Pro, Macbook, and two phones,

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:32.220
this yields 37-39 tokens a second at 60,000 contacts with every weight kept in VRAM or Unified

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:32.640
memory.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.840
The first PC holds layers 0-9 plus the output layer and the draft head.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.520
The Macbook holds layers 10-29.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.720
The second PC holds layers 30-47.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:50.420
Phone's handle expert selection for layers 10-18 over USB-C, while the Mac keeps the hottest

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:51.840
experts in its own memory.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:58.020
That draft head has to beat the extra PCIe and USB-C latency as the window grows, and

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:01.920
once acceptance drops under about 55% the quality edge is gone.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:08.560
The layout serves 69.6000 context natively before key value cash pressure forces a second

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:13.880
configuration that moves two layers back to the first PC and keeps 8-bit key value on

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.860
the Mac and phones.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:20.540
Every change is exact by construction except the Mac's expert cache, which adds partial

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.840
sums in a different order.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:26.120
The KL check against a reference has not yet been run on today's changes.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:31.560
The pattern pays off on mixed kits that already sit on your desk and need long-context decode.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:37.300
When the whole model fits in 24GB and you would rather keep the graph simple, cache experts

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.760
on one GPU instead.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.440
Stepping back from today's local checkpoints,

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:44.560
the past seven days were dominated by agent harnesses

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.480
and cheaper long-context inference.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.580
NVIDIA committed $250 million in UK compute

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.140
for agent-safety research over five years.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.600
Pause token key value compression

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.600
shrank cash 3.5 times

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.620
and sped H100 inference 3.2 times on long math problems.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.240
Yesterday, perplexity opened sourced

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:10.260
its firecracker micro-vm sandbox, giving builders a self-hostable isolation layer for long-running

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:11.140
agent tasks.

00:11:12.121 --> 00:11:17.701
Before we go, a second layout for the five device Quinn 3.8 Flash Next that reaches

00:11:17.701 --> 00:11:21.241
full 262,000 context is already in testing.

00:11:21.841 --> 00:11:23.601
That's models and agents for today.

